.TH BYTE_TRIMR 3
.SH NAME
byte_trimr \- trim trailing characters from a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_trimr(const char* " x ", size_t " n ", const char* " trimchars ", unsigned int " trimcharslen ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_trimr
scans the byte array
.I x
of length
.I n
from right to left to find the length of the prefix that does not end with any of the characters specified in
.IR trimchars .
.PP
The function iterates backwards from the end of the array, discarding any bytes found in the
.I trimchars
set (of length
.IR trimcharslen ). The process stops as soon as a byte is encountered that is not in the set, or when the entire array is exhausted.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes remaining in the prefix after trailing characters in
.I trimchars
have been removed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_chr (3)